# Git commits — no AI co-author

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any Cursor/AI co-author trailer) to commit messages.
- When creating commits, use only the user's authorship — no co-author lines.
- Before pushing, verify recent commits do not contain Cursor co-author trailers; amend or rewrite if needed (only when safe and user-approved).
